126447	126570	126444	126444	he	6774	" the first thing required of the criminal prosecutor was to prove unequivocally that the crime libelled had actually been committed , which lawyers called proving the _ corpus delicti . _ But this statute , made doubtless with the best intentions , and under the impulse of a just horror for the unnatural crime of infanticide , ran the risk of itself occasioning the worst of murders , the death of an innocent person , to atone for a supposed crime which may never have been committed by anyone . He was so far from acknowledging the alleged probability of the child 's violent death , that he could not even allow that there was evidence of its having ever lived . "
